the community center

00:20:55.080 --> 00:21:00.200
taken in isolation is compliant with the Andover Plan of Conservation and Development.

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:08.360
But in planning for this, we can't ignore the intended location of the center and the subsequent change to our zoning regulations.

00:21:10.365 --> 00:21:14.365
As a resident and a member of this commission, I believe we have the responsibility

00:21:14.365 --> 00:21:20.045
to make sure it's completed in such a way as to protect the school's interests and responsibilities

00:21:20.445 --> 00:21:21.885
while also allowing

00:21:22.045 --> 00:21:22.765
the construction

00:21:23.160 --> 00:21:24.600
of a community center.

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:28.680
I have concerns about changing the zoning regulations

00:21:28.840 --> 00:21:33.800
to delete schools from the list of special permit uses in the ARRD

00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:36.520
zone and substituting municipal land uses.

00:21:37.485 --> 00:21:40.925
I would much prefer to keep the listing for schools

00:21:41.005 --> 00:21:44.285
and add a municipal land uses

00:21:44.365 --> 00:21:46.365
to that special permit list.

00:21:47.645 --> 00:21:49.005
So we'd have both.

00:21:50.365 --> 00:21:51.485
I have three

00:21:52.270 --> 00:21:54.510
reasons for my beliefs on this.

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:57.950
One is that the Connecticut General Statute

00:21:58.350 --> 00:22:00.030
number ten-two

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:02.670
20 requires that the Board of Education

00:22:03.070 --> 00:22:03.790
shall

00:22:04.030 --> 00:22:07.310
have charge of the schools of its respective school district

00:22:07.605 --> 00:22:13.125
shall make a continuing study of the need for school facilities and of long term school building programs,

00:22:13.605 --> 00:22:19.845
and shall have the care and maintenance and operation of buildings, lands, apparatus, and other properties used for school purposes,

00:22:20.485 --> 00:22:21.045
unquote.

00:22:21.920 --> 00:22:26.880
That requires that school properties kept separate from other town owned property.

00:22:27.520 --> 00:22:31.600
And that's one reason why I think we should have a separate zoning use.

00:22:32.480 --> 00:22:34.880
Another concern, number two,

00:22:35.440 --> 00:22:38.645
the removal of the, quote, school identifier

00:22:38.645 --> 00:22:40.805
and lumping it in with municipal

00:22:40.805 --> 00:22:45.125
is that while school is a municipal building, it does not mean public access

00:22:46.005 --> 00:22:48.565
as would be expected in other municipal buildings

00:22:49.040 --> 00:22:52.640
and is what's intended in the proposed definition.

00:22:53.680 --> 00:22:58.160
Today, there's a great need for safety and security of the school buildings and property.

00:22:58.880 --> 00:23:02.080
As we've seen in the past few years, during the conversations

00:23:02.720 --> 00:23:04.800
about a senior center

00:23:04.735 --> 00:23:07.295
possibly using some school classrooms,

00:23:07.615 --> 00:23:13.695
the parents in Andover were very concerned about keeping their children safe in school and wanting it separate.

00:23:15.375 --> 00:23:16.175
The third thing,

00:23:17.220 --> 00:23:18.340
the proposed

00:23:18.340 --> 00:23:21.780
addition to Section 24 lists municipal

00:23:21.780 --> 00:23:25.940
land uses, buildings, structures, and the uses of the town of Andover

00:23:26.180 --> 00:23:28.900
or any regional public agency of which it's a member,

00:23:29.505 --> 00:23:34.625
but not including public uses by other agencies or entities compared to public, unquote.

00:23:35.985 --> 00:23:37.185
As the Connecticut

00:23:37.425 --> 00:23:42.545
General Statute requires the Board of Ed to have charge of the buildings and lands,

00:23:43.110 --> 00:23:46.630
I think there's a definite requirement for a separate identifier

00:23:46.710 --> 00:23:48.870
to be in the special permit uses.

00:23:49.430 --> 00:23:51.030
So that's

00:23:51.190 --> 00:23:53.750
why I feel we need to keep

00:23:54.390 --> 00:23:56.070
a school identifier,

00:23:56.070 --> 00:23:58.150
not just have it all lumped in with municipal.

